<title>UK: Sullom Voe oil liftings fall, most stay in Europe.</title>
<headline>Sullom Voe oil liftings fall, most stay in Europe.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brent Blend crude oil loadings from Britain's Sullom Voe terminal fell to 654,857 tonnes in the week to May 6, from 829,870 tonnes the previous week, Shetland Islands Marine Operations said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Of the total, only 92,310 tonnes went to the U.S. and the remainder stayed in Europe.</p>
